{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"language":"python","display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.16","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"competition","sourceId":170484},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":20783153}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/omidsakaki1370/name-that-llm-style-qwen-hybrid?scriptVersionId=369660289\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# **Cell 1: Problem Statement & Approach**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Name That LLM: Hybrid Baseline (Style + Qwen Embeddings)\n\n## 1. Problem Statement\nThis notebook attributes text passages to one of 18 language models. The key challenge is that test prompts are unseen, so we must avoid topic memorization. The evaluation metric is **Balanced Accuracy**.\n\n## 2. Approach: Hybrid Features\nWe leverage the **Prism Feature Atlas** , a pre-computed feature workbench that provides:\n- **468 style features**: punctuation, vocabulary, layout, etc.\n- **Frozen Qwen3-8B hidden states**: mean-pooled representations from layers 6 and 8.\n- **Fixed prompt-disjoint folds**: five folds where prompts never cross between train and validation.\n\nBy concatenating style and Qwen features and training a simple Logistic Regression, we capture both stylistic and semantic fingerprints without GPU memory constraints.\n\n## 3. Expected Performance\nAccording to the Atlas documentation, the combination of Qwen 8B layers (6, 8) and style features achi